import ConverterPage from '../components/ConverterPage.astro';
---

<ConverterPage
  path="/preeti-to-unicode"
  lede="Paste Preeti font Nepali on the left and get Unicode Devanagari on the right, once the Preeti layout has been mapped."
>
  <h2>Preeti is Nepali, not Hindi</h2>
  <p>
    Preeti is to Nepali roughly what Kruti Dev is to Hindi: the legacy font that
    a generation of government offices, newspapers and schools typed in, still
    embedded in older documents. It uses the same Devanagari script, which is
    why it looks familiar, but it is a different language with a different
    keyboard layout.
  </p>
  <p>
    That matters for accuracy. Nepali uses conjuncts and vowel combinations that
    Hindi does not, so a Preeti converter built on the Hindi map would be wrong
    in exactly the places Nepali differs from Hindi. This one will be built and
    tested against real Nepali documents before it goes live.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
